  "result": "Done! I've implemented credit notes for the invoicing system. Here's what was added:\n\n**Created src/credits.js:**\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` \u2014 creates a refund credit note\n  - Validates invoice is not draft (NOT_ISSUED)\n  - Validates date is a real date (DATE_INVALID)\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Prevents credit exceeding invoice total (CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n  - Returns `{ number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }`\n  - Numbers have CN prefix (CN-YYYY-NNNN) with separate counter from invoices\n  - Never mutates input\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code\n\n**Created test/credits.test.js:**\n- 19 comprehensive test cases covering all validation rules, counter logic, year resets, and edge cases\n\n**Results:**\n- All 184 tests passing (19 new credit note tests + 165 existing)\n- Credit notes work on issued, partially_paid, and paid invoices only\n- Separate numbering system ensures CN-* and INV-* numbers don't conflict",
